There are two parts to BlurHash. The first is a method that will extract the image from the URL and the second is a method that will generate a short string for the image.

On the first part, the URL of the image is passed as an argument. The URL can be either a relative URL or an absolute URL. The relative URL will be passed as the second argument. The image is stored in a local variable called img. The function will return an empty string if the URL does not contain an image.

The main function will either return the image or an empty string.

The function to generate a placeholder string for the image is called blurHash. It takes a string and returns a string that contains the image.

publicfunction blurHash(string url) {
// take an image
img.setAttribute("src", url);
return img;
}

